menu "Denon/Spotify Controller"

config DSC_FACTORY_TEST
    bool "Build factory test mode instead of the application"
    default n
    help
        Manufacturing hardware exerciser (docs/SECURITY.md §7b). Must never
        be enabled in a shipping build -- tools/check_release.py fails a
        production profile that has this set.

config DSC_PROV_AP_SSID_PREFIX
    string "Provisioning SoftAP SSID prefix"
    default "DSC-Setup"
    help
        net_wifi appends a MAC-derived suffix (docs/SECURITY.md §5). Read by
        app_wiring, injected into net_wifi_cfg_t -- net_wifi.c itself never
        references a CONFIG_ symbol directly.

config DSC_SNTP_SERVER
    string "SNTP server"
    default "pool.ntp.org"
    help
        Read by app_wiring, injected into net_time_cfg_t.

config DSC_OTA_MANIFEST_URL
    string "OTA manifest URL"
    default "https://ota.example.com/manifest.json"
    help
        Read by app_wiring, injected into svc_ota_cfg_t. docs/PLATFORM.md §2.3.

config DSC_OTA_FORCE_CHECK_ON_BOOT
    bool "Check for OTA update immediately on boot (dev convenience)"
    default n
    help
        Skips the randomised daily-check wait for the first check this
        boot. Never set in a production profile.

config DSC_TEST_FORCE_HEALTH_GATE_TIMEOUT
    bool "Force the post-OTA health gate to time out (test only)"
    default n
    help
        Suppresses the HEALTH_COND_BOOT_COMPLETE report so the health gate
        can never reach PASS, only TIMED_OUT after its window -- exists
        solely to exercise the automatic-rollback path on real hardware
        (docs/ROADMAP.md Tier 7's rollback proof). Must never be enabled
        in a shipping build -- tools/check_release.py fails a production
        profile that has this set.

config DSC_DENON_DEBUG_CONSOLE
    bool "Start a UART debug console for exercising svc_denon (dev convenience)"
    default n
    help
        docs/ROADMAP.md Phase 3's "crude debug UI" bullet, implemented as
        an esp_console REPL over UART instead of on-screen text -- no
        hal_display/LVGL bring-up exists yet (Phase 5 scope). Commands:
        denon status|host|power|volume|mute|input|mode|fuzz. Not a
        production feature -- tools/check_release.py fails a production
        profile that has this set, same as DSC_FACTORY_TEST.

config DSC_DENON_SELFTEST
    bool "Run a scripted svc_denon self-test after boot (test only)"
    default n
    help
        Once the link reaches CONNECTED_TELNET/CONNECTED_HTTP, submits a
        scripted sequence of real intents (power/input/volume/mute/mode,
        including a request above volume_limit_max to prove the safety
        clamp holds) through the real intent queue, then a fuzzed burst of
        volume intents -- docs/ROADMAP.md Phase 3's exit criterion, on real
        hardware. Exists because scripting interactive console input over
        this board's native USB-CDC port proved unreliable from Windows;
        this needs only read-only UART capture to verify. Must never be
        enabled in a shipping build -- tools/check_release.py fails a
        production profile that has this set, same as DSC_FACTORY_TEST.

endmenu
